{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DMYEkSNnx5z2HtNjQuGknA","type":"tool_result","content":"1\texport interface BlogPost {\n2\t  slug: string;\n3\t  title: string;\n4\t  excerpt: string;\n5\t  content: string; // HTML string\n6\t  date: string; // YYYY-MM-DD\n7\t  category: string;\n8\t  author: string;\n9\t  readTime: string;\n10\t  readingTimeMinutes: number;\n11\t  tags: string[];\n12\t  featuredImage: string;\n13\t}\n14\t\n15\t/** Compute reading time from HTML content (200 wpm, minimum 1 min). */\n16\tfunction computeReadingTime(html: string): number {\n17\t  const text = html.replace(/<[^>]+>/g, \" \").replace(/\\s+/g, \" \").trim();\n18\t  const wordCount = text.split(\" \").filter(Boolean).length;\n19\t  return Math.max(1, Math.ceil(wordCount / 200));\n20\t}\n21\t\n22\t/** Converts a category label to a URL-safe slug. e.g. \"Food & Drink\" → \"food-drink\" */\n23\texport function categoryToSlug(category: string): string {\n24\t  return category\n25\t    .toLowerCase()\n26\t    .replace(/[^a-z0-9\\s]/g, \"\")\n27\t    .trim()\n28\t    .replace(/\\s+/g, \"-\");\n29\t}\n30\t\n31\t/** Converts a category slug back to a display label, or returns null if not found. */\n32\texport function slugToCategory(slug: string): string | null {\n33\t  const found = blogPosts.find((p) => categoryToSlug(p.category) === slug);\n34\t  return found ? found.category : null;\n35\t}\n36\t\n37\t/** All unique categories in the blog. */\n38\texport function getUniqueCategories(): string[] {\n39\t  return [...new Set(blogPosts.map((p) => p.category))];\n40\t}\n41\t\n42\tconst rawPosts: Omit<BlogPost, \"readingTimeMinutes\">[] = [\n43\t  {\n44\t    slug: \"ultimate-jb-food-guide-backpackers\",\n45\t    title: \"The Ultimate Johor Bahru Food Guide for Backpackers (2026)\",\n46\t    excerpt:\n47\t      \"From RM5 hawker meals to legendary seafood spots — everything a budget traveller needs to eat their way through JB like a local.\",\n48\t    date: \"2026-02-20\",\n49\t    category: \"Food & Drink\",\n50\t    author: \"Pelangi Team\",\n51\t    readTime: \"8 min read\",\n52\t    tags: [\"johor-bahru\", \"food\", \"backpacker\", \"budget-travel\", \"malaysia\", \"hawker\"],\n53\t    featuredImage: \"/images/blog/jb-food-guide.jpg\",\n54\t    content: `\n55\t<h2>Why JB Is a Backpacker's Food Paradise</h2>\n56\t<p>Johor Bahru sits at the crossroads of Malay, Chinese, Indian, and Peranakan culinary traditions — and the prices are absurdly low. A full meal at a hawker centre runs RM5–12, a pulled tea costs RM2, and the quality of food rivals cities ten times its size. For backpackers crossing the border from Singapore, where a similar meal costs SGD8–15, JB feels like a food revelation.</p>\n57\t\n58\t<p>The city doesn't have Michelin stars or Instagram-bait restaurants. What it has is better: generations-old recipes, family-run stalls, and an eating culture where quality is the only way to survive. If you're staying at <a href=\"/rooms\">Pelangi Capsule Hostel in Taman Pelangi</a>, you're in one of the best food neighbourhoods in the city.</p>\n59\t\n60\t<h2>Breakfast: The Malaysian Way</h2>\n61\t<p><strong>Roti canai</strong> is the quintessential Malaysian breakfast — flaky, buttery flatbread torn by hand and dipped into dhal or fish curry. Every mamak (Indian-Muslim coffee shop) makes it, and it costs RM1.50–3. Pair it with a <strong>teh tarik</strong> (pulled milk tea, RM2) and you've got a breakfast that costs less than a Singapore MRT ride.</p>\n62\t\n63\t<p>If you want something heartier, try <strong>nasi lemak</strong> — coconut rice served with sambal chilli, fried anchovies, peanuts, cucumber, and a hard-boiled egg. The stall versions, wrapped in banana leaf, run RM3–5 and are available from dawn. For the adventurous, <strong>nasi kerabu</strong> (blue-coloured herbed rice) appears at Malay stalls and is worth seeking out.</p>\n64\t\n65\t<h2>Lunch: Hawker Centre Essentials</h2>\n66\t<p>JB's hawker centres are the backbone of the city's food culture. At lunch, every centre buzzes with office workers, families, and the occasional bewildered tourist who can't believe the prices. Head to <strong>Sik Bao Sin</strong> near Taman Pelangi for mixed rice — point at whatever looks good behind the glass, and the uncle will pile your plate for RM5–8.</p>\n67\t\n68\t<p>For noodle lovers, <strong>mee rebus</strong> is a Johorean specialty: yellow noodles in a thick, slightly sweet potato-based gravy, topped with boiled egg, tofu, and fried shallots. It's hearty, warming, and unlike anything you'll find elsewhere in Malaysia. <strong>Laksa Johor</strong> is even more distinctive — it uses spaghetti-like noodles instead of rice noodles, swimming in a rich fish-based curry. It's divisive, but locals are fiercely proud of it.</p>\n69\t\n70\t<p>Check our <a href=\"/guide\">JB Travel Guide</a> for a walking map of the best hawker centres within reach of the hostel.</p>\n71\t\n72\t<h2>Dinner: Seafood and Night Markets</h2>\n73\t<p><strong>San Low Seafood</strong>, a five-minute walk from Pelangi Capsule, is legendary among locals for its <strong>San Lou Bee Hoon</strong> — dry-fried vermicelli with prawns, egg, and a savoury soy glaze. The dish looks simple but the wok technique is masterful. Budget RM15–25 per person for a seafood dinner here, which is still a fraction of Singapore prices.</p>\n74\t\n75\t<p>If you prefer street food, JB's night markets (pasar malam) are unmissable. <strong>Taman Sentosa Night Market</strong> runs Thursday and Sunday nights and stretches for hundreds of metres: satay sticks (RM0.60 each), lok-lok (skewered meats dipped in boiling broth, RM1–2 per stick), martabak (stuffed pancakes), and fresh coconut water. Budget RM15–25 for a full night market feast.</p>\n76\t\n77\t<h2>Snacks and Drinks</h2>\n78\t<p><strong>Otak-otak</strong> — spiced fish paste wrapped in banana leaf and grilled over charcoal — is sold by roadside vendors for RM1–2 per piece. Buy five and eat them walking. <strong>Kuih</strong> (bite-sized Malay cakes and sweets) appear at morning markets and cost RM0.50–1 each. Try <strong>kuih lapis</strong> (rainbow layered cake) and <strong>ondeh-ondeh</strong> (pandan balls filled with palm sugar).</p>\n79\t\n80\t<p>For drinks, the <strong>teh tarik</strong> (pulled tea) is an art form. Watch the vendor pour boiling tea between two cups from arm's length, creating a frothy, perfectly mixed drink. <strong>Cham</strong> (coffee mixed with tea) is another local favourite. Fresh sugarcane juice costs RM3 and is the best remedy for JB's tropical heat.</p>\n81\t\n82\t<h2>Budget Breakdown</h2>\n83\t<p>Here's what a day of eating in JB actually costs:</p>\n84\t<ul>\n85\t  <li><strong>Breakfast:</strong> Roti canai + teh tarik — RM5</li>\n86\t  <li><strong>Lunch:</strong> Hawker centre mixed rice — RM8</li>\n87\t  <li><strong>Snack:</strong> Otak-otak + sugarcane juice — RM5</li>\n88\t  <li><strong>Dinner:</strong> Night market feast — RM20</li>\n89\t  <li><strong>Total:</strong> RM38 per day (approximately SGD11 or USD8)</li>\n90\t</ul>\n91\t\n92\t<p>That's three full meals, snacks, and drinks for less than the cost of one restaurant meal in Singapore. This is why backpackers who discover JB's food scene never want to leave.</p>\n93\t\n94\t<p>Ready to eat your way through JB? <a href=\"/book\">Book a capsule at Pelangi</a> and start your food adventure in one of the best eating neighbourhoods in the city.</p>\n95\t`,\n96\t  },\n97\t  {\n98\t    slug: \"singapore-to-jb-day-trip-causeway-guide\",\n99\t    title: \"Singapore to JB Day Trip Guide: How to Cross the Causeway (2026)\",\n100\t    excerpt:\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"80d00f4c-4638-42b3-9c87-be548860870f","uuid":"88e287f6-251d-402d-8fd2-847856e29676","timestamp":"2026-04-14T05:15:42.509Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\Jyue\\Documents\\1-projects\\Software Projects\\pelangi-website\\site\\src\\data\\blog\\posts.ts","content":"export interface BlogPost {\n  slug: string;\n  title: string;\n  excerpt: string;\n  content: string; // HTML string\n  date: string; // YYYY-MM-DD\n  category: string;\n  author: string;\n  readTime: string;\n  readingTimeMinutes: number;\n  tags: string[];\n  featuredImage: string;\n}\n\n/** Compute reading time from HTML content (200 wpm, minimum 1 min). */\nfunction computeReadingTime(html: string): number {\n  const text = html.replace(/<[^>]+>/g, \" \").replace(/\\s+/g, \" \").trim();\n  const wordCount = text.split(\" \").filter(Boolean).length;\n  return Math.max(1, Math.ceil(wordCount / 200));\n}\n\n/** Converts a category label to a URL-safe slug. e.g. \"Food & Drink\" → \"food-drink\" */\nexport function categoryToSlug(category: string): string {\n  return category\n    .toLowerCase()\n    .replace(/[^a-z0-9\\s]/g, \"\")\n    .trim()\n    .replace(/\\s+/g, \"-\");\n}\n\n/** Converts a category slug back to a display label, or returns null if not found. */\nexport function slugToCategory(slug: string): string | null {\n  const found = blogPosts.find((p) => categoryToSlug(p.category) === slug);\n  return found ? found.category : null;\n}\n\n/** All unique categories in the blog. */\nexport function getUniqueCategories(): string[] {\n  return [...new Set(blogPosts.map((p) => p.category))];\n}\n\nconst rawPosts: Omit<BlogPost, \"readingTimeMinutes\">[] = [\n  {\n    slug: \"ultimate-jb-food-guide-backpackers\",\n    title: \"The Ultimate Johor Bahru Food Guide for Backpackers (2026)\",\n    excerpt:\n      \"From RM5 hawker meals to legendary seafood spots — everything a budget traveller needs to eat their way through JB like a local.\",\n    date: \"2026-02-20\",\n    category: \"Food & Drink\",\n    author: \"Pelangi Team\",\n    readTime: \"8 min read\",\n    tags: [\"johor-bahru\", \"food\", \"backpacker\", \"budget-travel\", \"malaysia\", \"hawker\"],\n    featuredImage: \"/images/blog/jb-food-guide.jpg\",\n    content: `\n<h2>Why JB Is a Backpacker's Food Paradise</h2>\n<p>Johor Bahru sits at the crossroads of Malay, Chinese, Indian, and Peranakan culinary traditions — and the prices are absurdly low. A full meal at a hawker centre runs RM5–12, a pulled tea costs RM2, and the quality of food rivals cities ten times its size. For backpackers crossing the border from Singapore, where a similar meal costs SGD8–15, JB feels like a food revelation.</p>\n\n<p>The city doesn't have Michelin stars or Instagram-bait restaurants. What it has is better: generations-old recipes, family-run stalls, and an eating culture where quality is the only way to survive. If you're staying at <a href=\"/rooms\">Pelangi Capsule Hostel in Taman Pelangi</a>, you're in one of the best food neighbourhoods in the city.</p>\n\n<h2>Breakfast: The Malaysian Way</h2>\n<p><strong>Roti canai</strong> is the quintessential Malaysian breakfast — flaky, buttery flatbread torn by hand and dipped into dhal or fish curry. Every mamak (Indian-Muslim coffee shop) makes it, and it costs RM1.50–3. Pair it with a <strong>teh tarik</strong> (pulled milk tea, RM2) and you've got a breakfast that costs less than a Singapore MRT ride.</p>\n\n<p>If you want something heartier, try <strong>nasi lemak</strong> — coconut rice served with sambal chilli, fried anchovies, peanuts, cucumber, and a hard-boiled egg. The stall versions, wrapped in banana leaf, run RM3–5 and are available from dawn. For the adventurous, <strong>nasi kerabu</strong> (blue-coloured herbed rice) appears at Malay stalls and is worth seeking out.</p>\n\n<h2>Lunch: Hawker Centre Essentials</h2>\n<p>JB's hawker centres are the backbone of the city's food culture. At lunch, every centre buzzes with office workers, families, and the occasional bewildered tourist who can't believe the prices. Head to <strong>Sik Bao Sin</strong> near Taman Pelangi for mixed rice — point at whatever looks good behind the glass, and the uncle will pile your plate for RM5–8.</p>\n\n<p>For noodle lovers, <strong>mee rebus</strong> is a Johorean specialty: yellow noodles in a thick, slightly sweet potato-based gravy, topped with boiled egg, tofu, and fried shallots. It's hearty, warming, and unlike anything you'll find elsewhere in Malaysia. <strong>Laksa Johor</strong> is even more distinctive — it uses spaghetti-like noodles instead of rice noodles, swimming in a rich fish-based curry. It's divisive, but locals are fiercely proud of it.</p>\n\n<p>Check our <a href=\"/guide\">JB Travel Guide</a> for a walking map of the best hawker centres within reach of the hostel.</p>\n\n<h2>Dinner: Seafood and Night Markets</h2>\n<p><strong>San Low Seafood</strong>, a five-minute walk from Pelangi Capsule, is legendary among locals for its <strong>San Lou Bee Hoon</strong> — dry-fried vermicelli with prawns, egg, and a savoury soy glaze. The dish looks simple but the wok technique is masterful. Budget RM15–25 per person for a seafood dinner here, which is still a fraction of Singapore prices.</p>\n\n<p>If you prefer street food, JB's night markets (pasar malam) are unmissable. <strong>Taman Sentosa Night Market</strong> runs Thursday and Sunday nights and stretches for hundreds of metres: satay sticks (RM0.60 each), lok-lok (skewered meats dipped in boiling broth, RM1–2 per stick), martabak (stuffed pancakes), and fresh coconut water. Budget RM15–25 for a full night market feast.</p>\n\n<h2>Snacks and Drinks</h2>\n<p><strong>Otak-otak</strong> — spiced fish paste wrapped in banana leaf and grilled over charcoal — is sold by roadside vendors for RM1–2 per piece. Buy five and eat them walking. <strong>Kuih</strong> (bite-sized Malay cakes and sweets) appear at morning markets and cost RM0.50–1 each. Try <strong>kuih lapis</strong> (rainbow layered cake) and <strong>ondeh-ondeh</strong> (pandan balls filled with palm sugar).</p>\n\n<p>For drinks, the <strong>teh tarik</strong> (pulled tea) is an art form. Watch the vendor pour boiling tea between two cups from arm's length, creating a frothy, perfectly mixed drink. <strong>Cham</strong> (coffee mixed with tea) is another local favourite. Fresh sugarcane juice costs RM3 and is the best remedy for JB's tropical heat.</p>\n\n<h2>Budget Breakdown</h2>\n<p>Here's what a day of eating in JB actually costs:</p>\n<ul>\n  <li><strong>Breakfast:</strong> Roti canai + teh tarik — RM5</li>\n  <li><strong>Lunch:</strong> Hawker centre mixed rice — RM8</li>\n  <li><strong>Snack:</strong> Otak-otak + sugarcane juice — RM5</li>\n  <li><strong>Dinner:</strong> Night market feast — RM20</li>\n  <li><strong>Total:</strong> RM38 per day (approximately SGD11 or USD8)</li>\n</ul>\n\n<p>That's three full meals, snacks, and drinks for less than the cost of one restaurant meal in Singapore. This is why backpackers who discover JB's food scene never want to leave.</p>\n\n<p>Ready to eat your way through JB? <a href=\"/book\">Book a capsule at Pelangi</a> and start your food adventure in one of the best eating neighbourhoods in the city.</p>\n`,\n  },\n  {\n    slug: \"singapore-to-jb-day-trip-causeway-guide\",\n    title: \"Singapore to JB Day Trip Guide: How to Cross the Causeway (2026)\",\n    excerpt:","numLines":100,"startLine":1,"totalLines":843}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01LfBBcMQLykyMETrdBXe5ED","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Great! Now I understand the current state:\n\n1. **layout.tsx** (line 146): Already has `<link rel=\"alternate\" type=\"application/feed+json\" title=\"Pelangi Blog\" href=\"/feed.json\" />` \n2. **layout.tsx** (lines 59-61): metadata.alternates.types already includes both RSS and JSON Feed URLs\n3. **feed.xml/route.ts**: Exists and works, returns RSS 2.0 feed\n4. **posts.ts**: Contains blog post data with the required structure\n\nSo what still needs to be done:\n1. Check if RSS link tag is present in layout.tsx (it should be added if not)\n2. Create the JSON Feed 1.1 endpoint at /feed.json/route.ts\n\nLooking at the metadata in layout.tsx:\n- Lines 49-61: The `alternates` object has a `types` property that defines both feeds via metadata\n- However, the acceptance criteria asks for explicit `<link>` tags in the HTML head\n\nLooking at the head section:\n- Line 146: Already has `<link rel=\"alternate\" type=\"application/feed+json\"...>` for JSON Feed\n- But I don't see the RSS feed link tag! Let me check again...\n\nActually, checking the metadata.alternates.types (lines 58-61):\n```\ntypes: {\n  \"application/rss+xml\": \"https://pelangicapsulehostel.com/feed.xml\",\n  \"application/feed+json\": \"https://pelangicapsulehostel.com/feed.json\",\n},\n```\n\nThis uses the Next.js metadata API's `alternates.types` property, which Next.js converts to `<link rel=\"alternate\" ...>` tags automatically. However, looking at the head section, I see the JSON Feed link (line 146) but I need to check if the RSS link is there too.\n\nActually, looking at the head, I see on line 144:\n\n\n```html\n{/* JSON Feed: modern JSON alternative to RSS for blog syndication */}\n<link rel=\"alternate\" type=\"application/feed+json\" title=\"Pelangi Blog\" href=\"/feed.json\" />\n```\n\nThe JSON Feed link is explicitly in the head, but the RSS link tag isn't visible in the explicit head section. While metadata.alternates.types will auto-render both feeds, the acceptance criteria specifically requires adding the RSS `<link>` tag explicitly. Since the JSON feed is manually added, I should add the RSS link tag the same way for consistency.\n\nNext, I need to build the JSON Feed 1.1 endpoint at `/feed.json/route.ts`. The spec requires a version field pointing to `https://jsonfeed.org/version/1.1`, along with title, home_page_url, feed_url, description, language, and an items array. Each post object needs an id, title, content_html, date_published, and other optional fields like author and tags.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7385,"cache_read_input_tokens":60156,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7385},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"80d00f4c-4638-42b3-9c87-be548860870f","uuid":"4f629ac6-9f83-4346-a16e-7ebb697dba7c"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01LfBBcMQLykyMETrdBXe5ED","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Current State\n\nThe project has:\n- **layout.tsx**: Metadata already includes `alternates.types` for both feeds, and an explicit JSON Feed link tag (line 146), but **RSS link tag is missing** from the explicit head section\n- **feed.xml/route.ts**: Fully implemented RSS 2.0 endpoint that works\n- **posts.ts**: Blog post data with title, excerpt, content, date, category, author, tags, featuredImage\n\n## Problem Identified\n\n**US-265** requires:\n1. Add explicit `<link rel='alternate' type='application/rss+xml'...>` tag to layout.tsx head (for RSS auto-discovery)\n2. Create `/feed.json/route.ts` with JSON Feed 1.1 endpoint returning 10 most recent blog posts with proper structure\n\nCurrently:\n- RSS link is missing from explicit head (metadata.alternates.types handles it, but not the explicit tag)\n- JSON Feed endpoint doesn't exist\n\n## Planned Changes\n\n1. **site/src/app/layout.tsx**: Add RSS link tag to explicit head section (before or after the JSON Feed link)\n2. **site/src/app/feed.json/route.ts**: Create JSON Feed 1.1 endpoint with:\n   - Proper version/metadata\n   - Sort posts by date (newest first)\n   - Limit to 10 most recent\n   - Include required fields: id, title, content_html, date_published, author, url\n   - Optional: tags, summary (excerpt)\n\n<plan>\n{\n  \"files_to_create\": [\"site/src/app/feed.json/route.ts\"],\n  \"files_to_modify\": [\"site/src/app/layout.tsx\"],\n  \"functions_to_add\": [\"GET (feed.json route handler)\"],\n  \"estimated_loc\": 80\n}\n</plan>\n\nNow I'll execute the plan:"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7385,"cache_read_input_tokens":60156,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7385},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"80d00f4c-4638-42b3-9c87-be548860870f","uuid":"b1af062e-4f7a-4e9f-acc8-ddca16d42824"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01LfBBcMQLykyMETrdBXe5ED","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01ShNPGKDFrcquhXydtyoxx9","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"C:\\Users\\Jyue\\Documents\\1-projects\\Software Projects\\pelangi-website\\site\\src\\app\\layout.tsx","old_string":"        {/* JSON Feed: modern JSON alternative to RSS for blog syndication */}\n        <link rel=\"alternate\" type=\"application/feed+json\" title=\"Pelangi Blog\" href=\"/feed.json\" />","new_string":"        {/* RSS Feed: blog syndication */}\n        <link rel=\"alternate\" type=\"application/rss+xml\" title=\"Pelangi Blog\" href=\"/feed.xml\" />\n        {/* JSON Feed: modern JSON alternative to RSS for blog syndication */}\n        <link rel=\"alternate\" type=\"application/feed+json\" title=\"Pelangi Blog\" href=\"/feed.json\" />"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7385,"cache_read_input_tokens":60156,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7385},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"80d00f4c-4638-42b3-9c87-be548860870f","uuid":"0778d5ad-c8f4-4f50-8400-fd35bdf56782"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01ShNPGKDFrcquhXydtyoxx9","type":"tool_result","content":"The file C:\\Users\\Jyue\\Documents\\1-projects\\Software Projects\\pelangi-website\\site\\src\\app\\layout.tsx has been updated successfully."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"80d00f4c-4638-42b3-9c87-be548860870f","uuid":"354e986a-8896-41d7-b098-97e29135aa99","timestamp":"2026-04-14T05:15:57.592Z","tool_use_result":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\Jyue\\Documents\\1-projects\\Software Projects\\pelangi-website\\site\\src\\app\\layout.tsx","oldString":"        {/* JSON Feed: modern JSON alternative to RSS for blog syndication */}\n        <link rel=\"alternate\" type=\"application/feed+json\" title=\"Pelangi Blog\" href=\"/feed.json\" />","newString":"        {/* RSS Feed: blog syndication */}\n        <link rel=\"alternate\" type=\"application/rss+xml\" title=\"Pelangi Blog\" href=\"/feed.xml\" />\n        {/* JSON Feed: modern JSON alternative to RSS for blog syndication */}\n        <link rel=\"alternate\" type=\"application/feed+json\" title=\"Pelangi Blog\" href=\"/feed.json\" />","originalFile":"import type { Metadata } from \"next\";\nimport { Suspense } from \"react\";\nimport { Inter, Playfair_Display } from \"next/font/google\";\nimport Script from \"next/script\";\nimport { GoogleTagManager } from \"@next/third-parties/google\";\nimport \"./globals.css\";\nimport StructuredData from \"@/components/StructuredData\";\nimport { SpeedInsights } from \"@vercel/speed-insights/next\";\nimport { ChatWidget, MobileBookingBar, CookieConsent, AnalyticsProvider, BookingRecoveryBanner, MetaPixelProvider, TikTokPixelProvider, PauseAnimationsButton } from \"@/components/DynamicComponents\";\n\nconst GTM_ID = process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_GTM_ID ?? \"\";\n\nconst inter = Inter({ subsets: [\"latin\"], variable: \"--font-inter\" });\nconst playfair = Playfair_Display({ subsets: [\"latin\"], variable: \"--font-playfair\" });\n\n// TODO: Create OG image at /images/og-image.jpg (1200x630px) for optimal social sharing\n// Recommended: Feature hero image with \"Pelangi Capsule Hostel\" branding and \"From RM35/night\" text\n\nexport const metadata: Metadata = {\n  metadataBase: new URL(\"https://pelangicapsulehostel.com\"),\n  title: {\n    default: \"Pelangi Capsule Hostel | Budget Accommodation in Johor Bahru\",\n    template: \"%s | Pelangi Capsule Hostel\",\n  },\n  description: \"Experience Japanese-style capsule accommodation in Taman Pelangi, Johor Bahru. Budget-friendly hostel from RM35/night with free WiFi, 24/7 access, hot showers, and personal lockers. Perfect base for Singapore day trips - just 30 minutes from the border.\",\n  keywords: [\n    \"capsule hostel Johor Bahru\",\n    \"budget accommodation JB\",\n    \"hostel near Singapore\",\n    \"Taman Pelangi hostel\",\n    \"cheap hostel JB\",\n    \"backpacker accommodation Malaysia\",\n    \"Japanese capsule hotel JB\",\n    \"affordable hostel Johor\",\n    \"pod hostel Malaysia\",\n    \"budget stay near Singapore border\",\n  ],\n  robots: {\n    index: true,\n    follow: true,\n    googleBot: {\n      index: true,\n      follow: true,\n      \"max-video-preview\": -1,\n      \"max-image-preview\": \"large\",\n      \"max-snippet\": -1,\n    },\n  },\n  alternates: {\n    canonical: \"https://pelangicapsulehostel.com\",\n    languages: {\n      \"en\": \"https://pelangicapsulehostel.com\",\n      \"ms\": \"https://pelangicapsulehostel.com/ms/terma\",\n      \"x-default\": \"https://pelangicapsulehostel.com\",\n      \"zh-CN\": \"https://pelangicapsulehostel.com/zh\",\n      \"zh-Hans\": \"https://pelangicapsulehostel.com/zh\",\n    },\n    types: {\n      \"application/rss+xml\": \"https://pelangicapsulehostel.com/feed.xml\",\n      \"application/feed+json\": \"https://pelangicapsulehostel.com/feed.json\",\n    },\n  },\n  openGraph: {\n    title: \"Pelangi Capsule Hostel | Budget Accommodation in Johor Bahru\",\n    description: \"Japanese-style capsule accommodation from RM35/night in Taman Pelangi, JB. Free WiFi, 24/7 access, hot showers. Perfect for Singapore day trips!\",\n    url: \"https://pelangicapsulehostel.com\",\n    siteName: \"Pelangi Capsule Hostel\",\n    locale: \"en_MY\",\n    type: \"website\",\n    images: [\n      {\n        url: \"/images/og-image.png\",\n        width: 1200,\n        height: 630,\n        alt: \"Pelangi Capsule Hostel - Modern Japanese-style pods in Johor Bahru\",\n      },\n      {\n        url: \"/images/hero-main.webp\",\n        width: 1920,\n        height: 1080,\n        alt: \"Pelangi Capsule Hostel interior view\",\n      },\n    ],\n  },\n  twitter: {\n    card: \"summary_large_image\",\n    title: \"Pelangi Capsule Hostel | From RM35/night in JB\",\n    description: \"Japanese-style capsule hostel in Taman Pelangi, Johor Bahru. Budget-friendly, modern, and just 30 min from Singapore.\",\n    images: [\"/images/og-image.png\"],\n  },\n  verification: {\n    // Google Search Console — Replace with actual token from Add Property > HTML tag method\n    google: process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_VERIFICATION_TOKEN,\n    // Bing Webmaster Tools — Add token from Bing Webmaster Tools > Verify ownership > HTML tag method\n    // Once added here, Bing can auto-import GSC verification or use manual verification\n    other: process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_BING_VERIFICATION_TOKEN\n      ? { \"msvalidate.01\": process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_BING_VERIFICATION_TOKEN }\n      : undefined,\n  },\n  other: {\n    \"apple-mobile-web-app-status-bar-style\": \"black-translucent\",\n    // Pinterest domain verification — add token from Pinterest Developer Portal > Claim Website\n    ...(process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_PINTEREST_VERIFICATION_TOKEN\n      ? { \"p:domain_verify\": process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_PINTEREST_VERIFICATION_TOKEN }\n      : {}),\n  },\n};\n\nexport default function RootLayout({\n  children,\n}: Readonly<{\n  children: React.ReactNode;\n}>) {\n  return (\n    <html lang=\"en\" data-scroll-behavior=\"smooth\">\n      <head>\n        {/* Consent Mode v2: deny all consent parameters before GTM loads */}\n        <Script\n          id=\"consent-mode-defaults\"\n          strategy=\"beforeInteractive\"\n          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={{\n            __html: `\n              window.dataLayer = window.dataLayer || [];\n              function gtag(){window.dataLayer.push(arguments);}\n              gtag('consent', 'default', {\n                ad_storage: 'denied',\n                ad_user_data: 'denied',\n                analytics_storage: 'denied',\n                ad_personalization: 'denied',\n                functionality_storage: 'denied',\n                security_storage: 'granted'\n              });`,\n          }}\n        />\n        {/* Theme color: browser toolbar matches page background in light/dark mode */}\n        <meta name=\"theme-color\" content=\"#fafaf9\" media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" />\n        <meta name=\"theme-color\" content=\"#1c1917\" media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" />\n        {/* Preconnect: YouTube embed and Google Maps iframe */}\n        <link rel=\"preconnect\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com\" />\n        <link rel=\"preconnect\" href=\"https://www.google.com\" />\n        {/* OpenSearch: enables browser address bar search */}\n        <link rel=\"search\" type=\"application/opensearchdescription+xml\" title=\"Pelangi Hostel\" href=\"/opensearch.xml\" />\n        {/* llms.txt: AI crawler content guidance */}\n        <link rel=\"alternate\" type=\"text/plain\" href=\"/llms.txt\" />\n        {/* JSON Feed: modern JSON alternative to RSS for blog syndication */}\n        <link rel=\"alternate\" type=\"application/feed+json\" title=\"Pelangi Blog\" href=\"/feed.json\" />\n        {/* SVG favicon: sharp rendering on modern browsers, ICO/PNG fallbacks auto-detected from app/ */}\n        <link rel=\"icon\" type=\"image/svg+xml\" href=\"/favicon.svg\" />\n        {/* DNS-prefetch: Trip.com CDN for review/OTA images (cold path) */}\n        <link rel=\"dns-prefetch\" href=\"https://ak-d.tripcdn.com\" />\n        {/* Speculation Rules: prerender high-conversion pages on hover (Chrome/Edge only, ignored by others) */}\n        <script\n          type=\"speculationrules\"\n          dangerouslySetInnerHTML={{\n            __html: JSON.stringify({\n              prerender: [\n                {\n                  urls: [\"/book\", \"/rooms\", \"/gallery\"],\n                  eagerness: \"moderate\",\n                },\n              ],\n            }),\n          }}\n        />\n        {/* Preload LCP hero image — srcset matches Next.js Image optimization breakpoints */}\n        <link\n          rel=\"preload\"\n          as=\"image\"\n          fetchPriority=\"high\"\n          imageSrcSet=\"/_next/image?url=%2Fimages%2Fhero-final.png&w=640&q=75 640w, /_next/image?url=%2Fimages%2Fhero-final.png&w=750&q=75 750w, /_next/image?url=%2Fimages%2Fhero-final.png&w=828&q=75 828w, /_next/image?url=%2Fimages%2Fhero-final.png&w=1080&q=75 1080w, /_next/image?url=%2Fimages%2Fhero-final.png&w=1200&q=75 1200w, /_next/image?url=%2Fimages%2Fhero-final.png&w=1920&q=75 1920w, /_next/image?url=%2Fimages%2Fhero-final.png&w=2048&q=75 2048w, /_next/image?url=%2Fimages%2Fhero-final.png&w=3840&q=75 3840w\"\n          imageSizes=\"100vw\"\n        />\n      </head>\n      <body className={`${inter.variable} ${playfair.variable} pb-16 md:pb-0`}>\n        {GTM_ID && <GoogleTagManager gtmId={GTM_ID} />}\n        <a\n          href=\"#main-content\"\n          className=\"sr-only focus:not-sr-only focus:absolute focus:z-100 focus:top-4 focus:left-4 focus:px-4 focus:py-2 focus:bg-amber-700 focus:text-white focus:rounded-lg focus:font-medium focus:shadow-lg\"\n        >\n          Skip to main content\n        </a>\n        <StructuredData />\n        <Suspense>{children}</Suspense>\n        <MobileBookingBar />\n        <BookingRecoveryBanner />\n        <ChatWidget />\n        <PauseAnimationsButton />\n        <CookieConsent />\n        <AnalyticsProvider />\n        <MetaPixelProvider />\n        <TikTokPixelProvider />\n        <SpeedInsights />\n      </body>\n    </html>\n  );\n}\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":142,"oldLines":6,"newStart":142,"newLines":8,"lines":["         <link rel=\"search\" type=\"application/opensearchdescription+xml\" title=\"Pelangi Hostel\" href=\"/opensearch.xml\" />","         {/* llms.txt: AI crawler content guidance */}","         <link rel=\"alternate\" type=\"text/plain\" href=\"/llms.txt\" />","+        {/* RSS Feed: blog syndication */}","+        <link rel=\"alternate\" type=\"application/rss+xml\" title=\"Pelangi Blog\" href=\"/feed.xml\" />","         {/* JSON Feed: modern JSON alternative to RSS for blog syndication */}","         <link rel=\"alternate\" type=\"application/feed+json\" title=\"Pelangi Blog\" href=\"/feed.json\" />","         {/* SVG favicon: sharp rendering on modern browsers, ICO/PNG fallbacks auto-detected from app/ */}"]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_013om46GpSQmdbuvAeEy2TCN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Good! Now I need to create the JSON Feed 1.1 endpoint. Let me create the file with the proper structure.\n\nJSON Feed 1.1 requires:\n- version: \"https://jsonfeed.org/version/1.1\"\n- title: string\n- home_page_url: URL string\n- feed_url: URL string\n- description: string\n- language: string\n- items: array of objects\n\nEach item requires:\n- id: unique identifier (usually the URL or a UUID)\n- title: string\n- content_html: HTML content string\n- date_published: ISO 8601 datetime\n- author: object with at least \"name\" property\n- url: link to the post\n- tags: array of strings (optional)\n- summary: excerpt (optional)\n\nI'll model this after the RSS feed handler but with JSON Feed 1.1 structure.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1684,"cache_read_input_tokens":67541,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1684},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"80d00f4c-4638-42b3-9c87-be548860870f","uuid":"e085882b-38af-4cf3-a6d1-c5b607487cb4"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_013om46GpSQmdbuvAeEy2TCN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now I'll create the JSON Feed 1.1 endpoint:"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1684,"cache_read_input_tokens":67541,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1684},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"80d00f4c-4638-42b3-9c87-be548860870f","uuid":"ca989ff3-ed7e-4a32-bfbe-d638985c8c43"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_013om46GpSQmdbuvAeEy2TCN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_011FtMW4PX4SnGib6sGWZWqT","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"C:\\Users\\Jyue\\Documents\\1-projects\\Software Projects\\pelangi-website\\site\\src\\app\\feed.json\\route.ts","content":"import { blogPosts } from \"@/data/blog/posts\";\n\nexport async function GET() {\n  const baseUrl = \"https://pelangicapsulehostel.com\";\n\n  // Sort posts by date (newest first) and take top 10\n  const sortedPosts = [...blogPosts]\n    .sort((a, b) => new Date(b.date).getTime() - new Date(a.date).getTime())\n    .slice(0, 10);\n\n  // Build JSON Feed 1.1 structure\n  const feed = {\n    version: \"https://jsonfeed.org/version/1.1\",\n    title: \"Pelangi Capsule Hostel Blog\",\n    home_page_url: baseUrl,\n    feed_url: `${baseUrl}/feed.json`,\n    description:\n      \"Travel tips, guides, and stories for budget backpackers visiting Johor Bahru and Singapore\",\n    language: \"en-us\",\n    items: sortedPosts.map((post) => ({\n      id: `${baseUrl}/blog/${post.slug}`,\n      title: post.title,\n      content_html: post.content,\n      summary: post.excerpt,\n      date_published: new Date(post.date).toISOString(),\n      author: {\n        name: post.author,\n      },\n      url: `${baseUrl}/blog/${post.slug}`,\n      tags: post.tags,\n      image: post.featuredImage ? `${baseUrl}${post.featuredImage}` : undefined,\n    })),\n  };\n\n  return new Response(JSON.stringify(feed, null, 2), {\n    headers: {\n      \"Content-Type\": \"application/feed+json\",\n      \"Cache-Control\": \"public, s-maxage=3600, stale-while-revalidate=86400\",\n    },\n  });\n}\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1684,"cache_read_input_tokens":67541,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1684},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"80d00f4c-4638-42b3-9c87-be548860870f","uuid":"da26d8ee-20b5-4bec-a6eb-1fd057c23f9f"}
