{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Rx7vsGHipypAePyFi424sC","type":"tool_result","content":"1\timport { blogPosts } from \"@/data/blog/posts\";\n2\t\n3\texport async function GET() {\n4\t  const baseUrl = \"https://pelangicapsulehostel.com\";\n5\t\n6\t  const sortedPosts = [...blogPosts].sort(\n7\t    (a, b) => new Date(b.date).getTime() - new Date(a.date).getTime()\n8\t  );\n9\t\n10\t  const feed = {\n11\t    version: \"https://jsonfeed.org/version/1.1\",\n12\t    title: \"Pelangi Capsule Hostel Blog\",\n13\t    home_page_url: baseUrl,\n14\t    feed_url: `${baseUrl}/feed.json`,\n15\t    description:\n16\t      \"Travel tips, guides, and stories for budget backpackers visiting Johor Bahru and Singapore\",\n17\t    language: \"en\",\n18\t    authors: [\n19\t      {\n20\t        name: \"Pelangi Team\",\n21\t        url: baseUrl,\n22\t      },\n23\t    ],\n24\t    items: sortedPosts.map((post) => ({\n25\t      id: `${baseUrl}/blog/${post.slug}`,\n26\t      url: `${baseUrl}/blog/${post.slug}`,\n27\t      title: post.title,\n28\t      content_html: post.content,\n29\t      summary: post.excerpt,\n30\t      date_published: new Date(post.date).toISOString(),\n31\t      authors: [{ name: post.author }],\n32\t      tags: post.tags,\n33\t      language: \"en\",\n34\t      image: post.featuredImage.startsWith(\"http\")\n35\t        ? post.featuredImage\n36\t        : `${baseUrl}${post.featuredImage}`,\n37\t    })),\n38\t  };\n39\t\n40\t  return new Response(JSON.stringify(feed, null, 2), {\n41\t    headers: {\n42\t      \"Content-Type\": \"application/feed+json; charset=utf-8\",\n43\t      \"Cache-Control\": \"public, s-maxage=3600, stale-while-revalidate=86400\",\n44\t    },\n45\t  });\n46\t}\n47\t\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"80d00f4c-4638-42b3-9c87-be548860870f","uuid":"87f19150-896d-4189-a2bd-ce8739897ff3","timestamp":"2026-04-14T05:16:35.999Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\Jyue\\Documents\\1-projects\\Software Projects\\pelangi-website\\site\\src\\app\\feed.json\\route.ts","content":"import { blogPosts } from \"@/data/blog/posts\";\n\nexport async function GET() {\n  const baseUrl = \"https://pelangicapsulehostel.com\";\n\n  const sortedPosts = [...blogPosts].sort(\n    (a, b) => new Date(b.date).getTime() - new Date(a.date).getTime()\n  );\n\n  const feed = {\n    version: \"https://jsonfeed.org/version/1.1\",\n    title: \"Pelangi Capsule Hostel Blog\",\n    home_page_url: baseUrl,\n    feed_url: `${baseUrl}/feed.json`,\n    description:\n      \"Travel tips, guides, and stories for budget backpackers visiting Johor Bahru and Singapore\",\n    language: \"en\",\n    authors: [\n      {\n        name: \"Pelangi Team\",\n        url: baseUrl,\n      },\n    ],\n    items: sortedPosts.map((post) => ({\n      id: `${baseUrl}/blog/${post.slug}`,\n      url: `${baseUrl}/blog/${post.slug}`,\n      title: post.title,\n      content_html: post.content,\n      summary: post.excerpt,\n      date_published: new Date(post.date).toISOString(),\n      authors: [{ name: post.author }],\n      tags: post.tags,\n      language: \"en\",\n      image: post.featuredImage.startsWith(\"http\")\n        ? post.featuredImage\n        : `${baseUrl}${post.featuredImage}`,\n    })),\n  };\n\n  return new Response(JSON.stringify(feed, null, 2), {\n    headers: {\n      \"Content-Type\": \"application/feed+json; charset=utf-8\",\n      \"Cache-Control\": \"public, s-maxage=3600, stale-while-revalidate=86400\",\n    },\n  });\n}\n","numLines":47,"startLine":1,"totalLines":47}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01EKqj5mXe1v481ovDN8wz8r","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Great! The file already exists and it's already implementing JSON Feed 1.1, but there's an issue:\n\nThe current implementation:\n- Does NOT limit to 10 posts (story requirement: \"10 most recent blog posts\")\n- Has `authors` at feed level (optional, but not required)\n- Uses `authors` (plural) at item level instead of `author` (which the story acceptance criteria mentions)\n\nLet me check the acceptance criteria again:\n\"Create site/src/app/feed.json/route.ts that returns valid JSON Feed 1.1 with 10 most recent blog posts including title, content_html, date_published, and author\"\n\nAnd the verification: \"curl 'http://localhost:3000/feed.json' | jq '.items[0]' contains all required JSON Feed 1.1 fields\"\n\nSo I need to:\n1. Limit to 10 posts (add `.slice(0, 10)`)\n2. The JSON Feed 1.1 spec actually uses `authors` (plural) not `author`, but the story spec mentions \"author\". Let me check what the JSON Feed 1.1 spec says.\n\nActually, checking the JSON Feed 1.1 spec (https://www.jsonfeed.org/version/1.1/):\n- At the feed level: optional `authors` array\n- At the item level: optional `author` (singular) or `authors` (plural)\n\nThe current code uses `authors` (plural) at both levels. The story mentions \"author\" singular, but the code is correct per the spec. Let me just add the `.slice(0, 10)` to limit the posts.\n\nActually wait, let me re-read the current code. It has:\n- Line 18-22: `authors` at feed level\n- Line 31: `authors: [{ name: post.author }]` at item level\n\n\nThe JSON Feed 1.1 spec allows both `author` and `authors` formats at the item level, so the current implementation is valid. The main fix needed is adding `.slice(0, 10)` to restrict the output to exactly 10 posts as required.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":784,"cache_read_input_tokens":71169,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":784},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"80d00f4c-4638-42b3-9c87-be548860870f","uuid":"90f9a3e6-8f50-4bd6-8187-568b9c759aa8"}
